{"chunk_id": "e142738039e6", "text": "As the sacred Ganges follows King Bhagiratha across the land, a vast procession of gods, sages, spirits, and celestial beings accompanies the river. When the rushing waters flood the sacrificial ground of the sage Jahnu, he angrily drinks the entire river, astonishing the divine assembly. Appeased by their praise, he releases the river from his ear, giving Ganga the name Jahnavi, \"daughter of Jahnu.\" The river continues behind Bhagiratha\u2019s celestial chariot until it reaches the ashes of the sixty thousand sons of King Sagara in the underworld. When Ganga\u2019s waters touch them, they are purified and ascend to heaven. Brahma appears to declare Bhagiratha\u2019s success, granting the river his name Bhagirathi and immortalizing his achievement of redeeming his ancestors through perseverance and dharma.\nBhagiratha leads Ganga to his ancestors\u2019 ashes; Jahnu briefly drinks the river; the sons of Sagara are liberated and Brahma blesses Bhagiratha.\nThemes: ancestral redemption, sacred river Ganga, divine blessing, filial duty, cosmic purification", "vector": [0.0020643838215619326, -0.004770355299115181, -5.1942024583695456e-05, 0.029626067727804184, -0.0003652563027571887, 0.024918874725699425, -0.02858888916671276, 0.011076532304286957, -0.02264505997300148, -0.021913716569542885, -0.0024732714518904686, -0.0019031557021662593, 0.0071738166734576225, 0.008915744721889496, 0.0024849064648151398, -0.005797560792416334, 0.046353891491889954, -0.020065411925315857, 0.02741874009370804, 3.3275359783146996e-06, -0.010105839930474758, -0.0002632421674206853, 8.175674884114414e-05, 0.030796218663454056, -0.043056197464466095, 0.023363105952739716, 0.02551724575459957, -0.010398377664387226, 0.007592677138745785, 0.004102173261344433, -0.025956053286790848, -0.008902447298169136, -0.01954682171344757, 0.017778299748897552, 0.000493241474032402, 0.002285449067130685, -0.018589427694678307, -0.007486300077289343, 0.00595380272716